Each null spelling — `null` and `~` — is written as the bare word `null`, so the key reloads
as a real null and stays a clearable queue marker.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
retro: 2026-01-01
---
# Body
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md retro=null planned=~
-- exit --
0
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: retro=null, planned=~
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
retro: null
planned: null
---
# Body
